WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.258 --> 00:00:04.205
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:07.598
Give me one minute, and I'll show you

00:00:07.598 --> 00:00:09.549
how Cloud Data Fusion
can help you build

00:00:09.549 --> 00:00:12.375
data marts, data warehouses,
and data lakes fast.

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.655
Data Fusion is a fully managed,

00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:17.128
cloud-native enterprise data
integration service

00:00:17.128 --> 00:00:20.646
for ETL developers, data analysts,
and data engineers.

00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:24.667
It provides a visual point-and-click
interface to easily design,

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.942
deploy, and manage data pipelines.

00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:30.739
Data Fusion improves business
IT collaboration by providing

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:34.513
a unified user experience
for data wrangling and pipeline design.

00:00:34.723 --> 00:00:37.200
It's powered by the open source
project CDAP,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.305
making it a flexible and portable solution

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.551
for hybrid and multi-cloud environments.

00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:44.417
Data Fusion offers broad
connectivity options

00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:48.244
to on-prem or cloud data
from databases, mainframes, SaaS,

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:49.763
and enterprise applications.

00:00:50.096 --> 00:00:53.677
With built-in features around metadata,
Data Fusion helps with governance

00:00:53.677 --> 00:00:57.480
by providing insights into pipelines
through end-to-end pipeline lineage.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.577
To get started with Data Fusion,

00:00:59.577 --> 00:01:01.736
create an <i>Instance</i> in the Cloud Console

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.528
and then head into the UI
to visually wrangle data

00:01:04.528 --> 00:01:07.993
and design your pipelines,
as you profile, prepare, blend,

00:01:07.993 --> 00:01:09.670
enrich, and transform data.

00:01:09.981 --> 00:01:12.131
Finally, deploy and run your pipeline

00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:15.627
on automatically provisioned
Dataproc clusters with just a click.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.054
You can also schedule, monitor,
and manage your pipelines.

00:01:19.668 --> 00:01:21.668
Next time you're looking to accelerate

00:01:21.668 --> 00:01:24.752
the building of data marts,
data warehouses, and data lakes,

00:01:25.103 --> 00:01:26.803
take a look at Data Fusion.

00:01:29.177 --> 00:01:33.565
To learn more, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/data-fusion</i>

00:01:34.977 --> 00:01:36.477
♪ [music] ♪

